@prefix pm:      <https://pajew.ski/prima-materia/ontology#> .
@prefix pmc:     <https://pajew.ski/prima-materia/concepts/> .
@prefix pmp:     <https://pajew.ski/prima-materia/practices/> .
@prefix rdfs:    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix skos:    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .
@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .

#
# prima-materia - two searches in the Taulipang ethnography
#
# The first is the search the work was opened for, and it found more than the
# holding usually gets. The second was put to the same pages and came back with
# nothing, and the nothing is worth as much, because it fixes which kind of
# condition this transmission has and which it does not.
#

pmp:TaulipangDefectusSearch a pm:Searching ;
    rdfs:label "Whether the transmission names a condition under which the capacity is destroyed"@en, "Ob die Ueberlieferung eine Bedingung nennt, unter der das Vermoegen zerstoert wird"@de ;
    pm:searchedCorpus "Theodor Koch-Gruenberg, Vom Roroima zum Orinoco, Band III: Ethnographie (Stuttgart: Strecker und Schroeder, 1923), pp. 194-221" ;
    pm:searchedFor "Any sentence naming what would destroy, prevent or undo a capacity of this transmission, or what would show that an operation had not worked: a substance that disqualifies, a term after which nothing more comes, a repetition on failure, a defect in the operator, a sign of failure announced in advance. The question was put to this corpus rather than another because the holding is shortest of exactly this and because the registered transmissions outside the Eurasian contact space had so far yielded none of it." ;
    pm:searchTerms "The German body text of the part read was read continuously from the running head 194 to the running head 221, the chapter having been located by its running heads because the chapter headings are destroyed in the optical reading. It was then searched for verbrennen, abschneiden, niemals, nie mehr, verlieren, verliert, Kraft verlieren, misslingt, vergeblich, umsonst, nicht gelingen, unwirksam, Frist, Probe, Pruefung, Verbot, verboten, darf nicht, essen, trinken, Fasten, abbrechen, Gewitter, Regen. The page sequence of the running heads was checked before any page was cited." ;
    pm:searchOutcome pm:searchFoundPlace ;
    pm:searchYieldedNode pmc:TaulipangWoleleLeavesBurnTheThroat, pmc:TaulipangPiranhaCutsTheSkyLadder, pmc:TaulipangNoCureDuringRain, pmp:TaulipangZauberarztApprenticeship, pmc:TaulipangLongerStudyStrongerShaman, pmc:TaulipangNeverOneNoviceAlone, pmc:TaulipangMauariCrystalFallsIntoThePocket, pmc:TaulipangReleaseWhenManyHaveFallen, pmp:TaulipangSoulLeavesByTheHairCord, pmc:TaulipangSoulRetrievedByTheMaster, pmp:TaulipangJaguarTransformation, pmc:TaulipangJaguarCertifiedByTheBystanders, pmc:TaulipangTheTrunkWasEmpty, pmc:TaulipangSpellsNeedNoInitiation, pmc:TaulipangImmunityInferredFromTheAnimal ;
    pm:searchedBy "prima-materia, 2026-10-04" ;
    dcterms:date "2026-10-04" ;
    skos:note "Two conditions, and both are of the strong kind the search was shaped for. The leaves of wolele-yeg, brewed into the drink pelakali and forbidden for the whole apprenticeship, would burn the novice's whole throat so that he could never sing again; and piranha, the one food still forbidden after release, would cut the ladder to the sky so that he could never ascend again. Each names the substance, the mechanism and the faculty lost, each is announced in advance, and each is permanent. Between them they cover both faculties the office consists of."@en ;
    skos:note "A third find of a different kind: the cure is never performed during rain, and a thunderstorm breaking out during the work ends it at once, to be begun again from the beginning the following night. That is the only condition in the part read which lies outside both the practitioner and the person operated on, and it is the only one that carries a resumption rule."@en ;
    skos:note "The strongest single passage was not what the search was looking for. At pmc:TaulipangTheTrunkWasEmpty a practitioner reports an operation, a verification he performed on it - he locked the thing he had caught in a trunk and opened the trunk in the morning - and an empty result, which he then accounts for by the nature of what he had caught. The holding carries containers and residues applied to a performance by other people; this is the only one applied by the operator to himself, in private, with both halves reported by him."@en ;
    skos:note "What the two conditions do not establish, stated so that the find is not overstated. Neither is tested and neither is said ever to have happened to anybody. A prohibition with a cited consequence is a falsifiable claim and not a verified one, and no pm:Testing node is written for either; the botanical identification wolele-yeg would need is not in the passage, while the fish is identified by the recorder as Serrasalmo sp."@en .

pmp:TaulipangSignOfFailureSearch a pm:Searching ;
    rdfs:label "Whether a practitioner is ever told how to recognise that an operation did not work"@en, "Ob dem Vollzieher je gesagt wird, woran er erkennt, dass eine Verrichtung nicht gewirkt hat"@de ;
    pm:searchedCorpus "Theodor Koch-Gruenberg, Vom Roroima zum Orinoco, Band III: Ethnographie (Stuttgart: Strecker und Schroeder, 1923), pp. 194-221" ;
    pm:searchedFor "Whether the part read anywhere names a sign by which the practitioner or a bystander would know that a cure, a soul-journey or a transformation had failed; a number of attempts after which it is given up; or a condition in the operator or the material that accounts for an operation that produced nothing. This is the other half of the question above: not what destroys the capacity, but what shows that an exercise of it miscarried." ;
    pm:searchTerms "The same continuously read pages, searched for the terms listed at pmp:TaulipangDefectusSearch and in addition for Zeichen, erkennen, erkennt, umsonst, wirkungslos, half nicht, starb, Tod, gestorben, wiederholen, nochmals, von neuem, and for the numerals in the account of the cure. The three reported cases in the part read - the three deaths at Koimelemong, the empty trunk, the jaguar at the dance feast - were each read through for a sentence of this kind." ;
    pm:searchOutcome pm:searchFoundNothing ;
    pm:searchedBy "prima-materia, 2026-10-04" ;
    dcterms:date "2026-10-04" ;
    skos:note "Nothing, and the shape of the nothing is the finding. This transmission is unusually well supplied with conditions that disqualify a practitioner permanently and carries not one sign that a particular performance miscarried. The two are not the same instrument: a disqualification is about the man and is checked once, a sign of failure is about an occasion and would be checked every time."@en ;
    skos:note "Three places where such a sign could have stood and does not. Three men died of dysentery at Koimelemong while a Zauberarzt was singing over the sickness, and the account of it reports the wrestling and the empty trunk and says nothing about the deaths counting for or against the cure. The novices lie as if dead and their body wakes before their soul returns, which is an interval in which something could be read, and nothing is read in it. And a cure may run several nights in succession with no number given, so there is no count at which it ends."@en ;
    skos:note "The limit of the search. Twenty-eight printed pages of a volume of some four hundred, and none of the eleven spells, which are the one part of this corpus printed with its original wording and which carry, by the recorder's own description, an instruction for application at the end of each. If a sign of failure is anywhere in this corpus it is most likely there, and that is where the next run at it should go."@en .
